@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] contract-review-portability
The action reviews the supplied PR number in the caller's repository without requiring caller-local
review scripts, prompts, skills, a Node project, or `cc-check`; its tooling and review instructions
come from the action repository, and setup never executes package scripts from the inspected PR.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] contract-review-node-runtime
Review setup selects the Node.js version in the action revision's `cc-check/.nvmrc` for both local
action checkouts and remote action invocations.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-captured-context
Review context contains the captured request, merge base, comparison files, existing comments and
reviews, and passed action-tooling checks; those checks never claim to validate the inspected PR.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-progress
Each workflow run reports review progress in its own `Contract review (<run-id>)` commit status
on the inspected head, linked to that run; concurrent runs never overwrite one another's status.
Statuses distinguish running, completed, failed, and cancelled execution; success means the review
completed, not that it approves the PR.
